rock walls which reach far above your head.  The hills continue to rise above
you to the north and west.  Hundreds of stones clatter about your feet as you
walk here, the stone of the hills worn and broken down here by the ages.  Two
large rocks block your exit to the east, though perhaps it would be possible
to squeeze between them.
